{"title":"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> be integers greater than 2.  Prove that there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and a finite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/935c5514187e64b59e60dcedb07f40e000c70455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2, \\ldots, n_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201bdf656d0786716ddc15aa2e1bc9bbdaecd5e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54eeda6a2b7cf6cd1d13ade3c89387cf8b2e9a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_k = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de1ae34acc4ad9b08c69882a11937eebe823bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_in_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5610f0f6b26eb004047146d3580e95563364b6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i + n_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/5195e4207b21b1d5ec54801b99374c4af7799874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We may say that two integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are <i>connected</i> (and write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d786ee5077ed4deab9dd1361870b2f01bd8c3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />) if there exists such a sequence of integers as described in the problem.  For reference, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d4563ad8c3bc2ead402d6ffc50768b0269bf073a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leftrightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equivalence_relation\" title=\"Equivalence relation\">equivalence relation</a>: it is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflexive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Reflexive\">reflexive</a> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b8c61bef5119df824b58a5d81d0faeee356c830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"10\" />), <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetric\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Symmetric\">symmetric</a> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d786ee5077ed4deab9dd1361870b2f01bd8c3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b08427b0c30f6c691123a05daeb5a3f67e8253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leftrightarrow a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />), and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Transitive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Transitive\">transitive</a> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/55316d233e09d6c28511b7e3f2ff73c79460c153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow b \\leftrightarrow c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5a24d25e82a334bc7702705964ef9dd1d0c2b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" /> ).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that for any divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a75c578837c8ad0bff81dddae81f83ccc2df2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(d-1) + n = nd \\mid n^2(d-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa9c9c4a199bf92bd85b61c46c2a4af0e9fffdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(d-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.  It follows that in fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad32306bd40d75ebb061d0337c7cdeb15cdba6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(d-1)^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, for any nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26ef969ad94661906784e47ae386b95328a59a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(d-1) \\leftrightarrow n(d-1)(d-2) \\leftrightarrow \\cdots \\leftrightarrow n \\prod_{i=c}^{d-1}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"378\" height=\"51\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a6389a39fb489718360fca5e59a3860c6a322d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b65442489f64fb3c21224f6bb854a636a53e6d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, there exists some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a7d9776308d2d819668833eefef586cedf1b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-1)^{\\lambda} &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />.  Let\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a41d8cf761a9b2a56aec2751181cac372b4a954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = \\prod_{i=b}^{(b-1)^{\\lambda}}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"90\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed23568fa65f0eb25b681c36fa6e0848dacde79a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow \\prod_{i=b}^{a}i \\leftrightarrow (b-1)^{\\lambda} \\prod_{i=b}^{a}i \\leftrightarrow (b-1)^{\\lambda}  \\prod_{i=b}^{a}i \\cdot \\prod_{i=a+1}^{(b-1)^{\\lambda}-1} i = X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"440\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But we also have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0146b9f202eedafbdf3b0e66a846eb78834dfb57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leftrightarrow b(b-1)^{\\lambda} \\leftrightarrow b (b-1)^{\\lambda} \\prod_{i=b+1}^{(b-1)^{\\lambda}-1}i = X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"314\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e725e856a220645916960c4c0fa67f6470dbb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow X \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d786ee5077ed4deab9dd1361870b2f01bd8c3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We note that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95bacca4943530f2731806742baf6da91c60fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, for\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d295c7f9f2f8332dfc2a7592217cd3ba48cc589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(n-1) \\leftrightarrow n(n-1)(n-2) \\leftrightarrow n(n-2) \\leftrightarrow 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>It follows that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b94ea0cc3ac2d353695f157196aed47896fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/8217a1f3034d1bea0966ae932da408bfe296dd41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(n-1) \\leftrightarrow n(n-1)(n-2) \\leftrightarrow n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3) \\leftrightarrow 2(n-1)(n-2) \\leftrightarrow (n-1)(n-2) \\leftrightarrow (n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"841\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Thus all integers greater than 2 are connected.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd660dc23899ffa54e4bcc37c8edb39609dfb6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i + n_{i+1} \\mid n_in_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc98a141c825e41884fba721b36d79b48f216ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n_i + n_{i+1}) \\mid [(n_i + n_{i+1})n_i - n_in_{i+1}] = n_i^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"327\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Therefore for any divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3577eeb68e4db5a6cc4bbe996b134e17df1c003c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &gt; n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa28b5352cde8cdfd7b5e68f40190f2ac19aa52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c70c8ff41b00673f4f93ae95b44577d67578a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d - n_i \\leftrightarrow n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2cd546ffbb52fe8a7f8e4d1cb3ec38047627e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f1d0ab261281d39670267146e16b678c8bd502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a \\leftrightarrow 4a^2 - 4a = 4a(a-1) \\leftrightarrow 8a^2 - 4a(a-1) = 4a(a+1) \\leftrightarrow 4(a+1)^2 - 4a(a+1) = 4(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"743\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Also,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720d71dbb80df376795269bcc7a966cdc307f269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\leftrightarrow 4^2 - 4 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>This means that all positive multiples of 4 are connected.\n</p><p>Furthermore, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2cd546ffbb52fe8a7f8e4d1cb3ec38047627e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b635249ec46d28ba2eee634b170ec0ca3c5394a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a \\leftrightarrow 2a(a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which implies that every even number greater than 2 is connected to a multiple of 4.\n</p><p>Finally, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/761f953f34c7f838cd0742690928b86e9710a5ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6220a9e03165ad962c243d455ccf4e664396fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow a(a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3426cca6bb42be1336e940335f2db3062367be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is even, this means that all integers greater than or equal to 2 are connected to some even number.\n</p><p>Together, these imply that all integers greater than 2 are connected.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8284038292bba772df8ba50b204218242a5fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa9c9c4a199bf92bd85b61c46c2a4af0e9fffdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow n(d-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We say a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>safe</i> if for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f892b213bdf0eefb87c92595a6013b4115cd7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow kn$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.  Note that the product of two safe numbers is also a safe number.  Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />) to be the smallest divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that is greater than 2.  We will prove that 2 is safe, by strong induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />.  For the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/2801402309198acc537f4c3ab1e4fa4b071573e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debaab20f26517535f853feda9abcc4b02952ad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow (3-1)n = 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec843d988d8e595205f2ed7bea6142a53c593bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e45df722755bb6a531e566b963384f638d0a4e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f[n(f(n) - 1)] &lt; f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488d5b6ffe2fe19edf141e2723279df754981321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> must be less than all the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Thus the inductive hypothesis gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44b173cfe2f81eb484cc870351fa4c60e197553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[f(n) - 1]n \\leftrightarrow 2[f(n) - 1]n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"18\" />.  Furthermore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b653b6309037f125c8f3402d1d53516555c696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow [f(n)-1]n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4b198b8b8dc0aa405f56944055ec893a004e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n \\leftrightarrow 2[f(n)-1]n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, both from our initial note.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95bacca4943530f2731806742baf6da91c60fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We will now prove that every prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is safe, by strong induction.  We have already proven the base case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e129fbcb9c592946641c11f0c3eb03a078b4bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Now, for odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d58d0cd6161c8c4be4d6284f59ec576295093e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> is the product of odd primes less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d58d0cd6161c8c4be4d6284f59ec576295093e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> is safe.  Then we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e4999462a498801844315e7a320b24f91fd7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leftrightarrow (p+1)n \\leftrightarrow p(p+1)n \\leftrightarrow pn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Thus the induction is complete, and all primes are safe.\n</p><p>We have now shown that all integers greater than 1 are safe.  Specifically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are safe, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe4612a475e1a2eefa9fa88dfb9799ad808378c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow ab \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Similarly to the first solution, we observe that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43aa3bfcef1237d186b43d986999970e83714e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and any positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/8298c0ab96fa1090f51bc5371fca5cdafd70524c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1, \\ldots, e_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"11\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f5a86d40805fc44c2591ad00a1791b9e5044d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow a \\prod_{i=1}^{k}(a-i)^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"136\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We also note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d786ee5077ed4deab9dd1361870b2f01bd8c3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, then for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd1cf4235ebc92d36ca46cd6330bb568443a802f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ka \\leftrightarrow kb$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5d40b646472adbc665733e3b27077821040e8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b) \\mid (ab)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04abc8cd6d7d7d83d2bef57369e8833bc88d4e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(a+b) \\mid k^2(ab)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>It is sufficient to prove that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f3819b8679cbfc2ab2102f303c40c85d5c7e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e0fed86da976ddfaa0a286b59860364f30e1e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftrightarrow (a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is composite, then there exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c78ef61a6190f066522084854f891d03d2c269c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e441b1836a83d5d3666d52381f892d05b37d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1-m)(a-1-n) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />, and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd686d107a9e8e3830fcae08d59eb10b067e5f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1) \\leftrightarrow (a-1-m)(a-1-n) \\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(a-1-i) = a \\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(a-1-i) \\leftrightarrow a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"567\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>If, on the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is prime, then we use strong induction.  For the base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72e2e58a2ef8bb4eedd627c212f63bb8f507301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65933dc18b92d2226560fb74ec4b5f0ca0f86476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\leftrightarrow 3 \\leftrightarrow 3(3-1) = 6 \\leftrightarrow 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />.  Now, assuming that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb395390cae5209aa7a0216254cda07db6991cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and that this holds for all primes less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (we know it holds for all composites), it is sufficient to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dad2961428e22a0361bd9737b598357b26bb7c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1) \\leftrightarrow (a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2bddf56169e3d800f7a71d5d35d3196b35e3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> is composite and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/50188650e00b65dbf2897d55f8e5d9bf1367ea66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1) \\leftrightarrow a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />.  But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2bddf56169e3d800f7a71d5d35d3196b35e3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab66cc490be41469229525c5361c44f051372e87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> are both even, it suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3d5a408df771b2c0c2b14ff9125acf5a085fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2} \\leftrightarrow \\frac{a-1}{2} = \\frac{a+1}{2} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"220\" height=\"38\" />.  But this is true, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97439a3cb35d6366b2b48331bc36d5bb25cf1839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> either composite, or a prime less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and it is greater than 3, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38cf958f3236016549778542e3568fec9543ab6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus the induction is complete.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO\" title=\"2002 USAMO\">2002 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201218\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.778 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 612/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21095/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.426      1 -total\n 57.59%    7.156      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 39.63%    4.924      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4639:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201218 and revision id 69666. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}